<title>SOUTH KOREA: KIA DENIES TALKS OVER RENAULT PLANT.</title>
<headline>KIA DENIES TALKS OVER RENAULT PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Kia Motors Corp on Thursday said a purchase of a Belgian automobile assembly plant owned by French car maker Renault SA has never been discussed within the company or with Renault.</p>
<p>However, Kia Motors spokesman Jeun Sang-jin declined to comment on whether the car maker was interested in the buyout.</p>
<p>&quot;All Korean companies are interested. But there has been no discussion of a takeover within the company or with Renault,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
